From: fix session 2026-09-12
Subject: [PATCH 0034] wasm64: bias the helper retaddr by GETPC_ADJ (EL71 flash abort)

The wasm64 backend has no host return addresses, so every helper call is
preceded by a store of a synthetic retaddr into the thread-local
w64_tb_ptr that GETPC() reads (tcg/wasm64/tcg-target.h).  The value was
w64_pc(): the code-buffer offset *before* the call sequence is emitted.

cpu_unwind_data_from_tb() resolves a retaddr by walking the per-insn end
offsets for the first one strictly greater than (retaddr - GETPC_ADJ) —
a real backend's GETPC() is a return address, which always lies after
the call and therefore strictly inside the faulting insn's code range.
The wasm64 marker is not: for any guest insn whose generated code
*starts* with the helper call — every plain load/store whose address is
already in a register — the raw offset equals that insn's start, i.e.
the previous insn's end offset, and the unwind attributed the access to
the preceding guest instruction.  (For a helper call at the very start
of a TB the subtraction even underflowed past tb->tc.ptr, and
cpu_unwind_data_from_tb returned -1: no state restore at all.)

Everything that unwinds mid-TB then worked on the wrong insn.  The
visible failure was cpu_io_recompile(): it rewound the vCPU to the
*previous* guest insn and re-executed it, so an insn with a register
writeback ran twice.  The EL71 boot writes its flash file system through
a buffered program: `ldm r0!` before the first store to the flash
command region was re-executed, r0 ran 16 bytes past the source buffer,
the guest programmed the erased pattern into the write buffer and the
firmware aborted with ">>EXIT<< ExitCode: 0x0506 FILE: flash
ExitString: <line>:Prog:B3F78936:3" ~4 s into the boot.  S75/C81 do not
program flash during boot and never hit it; the TCI dist was unaffected
(tci_tb_ptr points at the current op, GETPC_ADJ bytes into the insn);
-accel tcg,one-insn-per-tb=on hid it (nothing precedes the insn), which
is why the lockstep gate — which forces one-insn-per-tb — stayed green.

Bias the marker by GETPC_ADJ so the subtraction lands exactly on the
insn's start offset, which the strict comparison attributes to that
insn.  The call sequence emitted after it is always longer than the
bias, so the marker never refers to the next insn either.

No measurable cost (the constant is folded into the existing store).
Verified: EL71 boots to the UI on dist-jit (flash trace now
byte-identical to the TCI dist through the buffered program), S75 and
KE800 unchanged, wasm64 lockstep clean.

diff --git a/tcg/wasm64/tcg-target.c.inc b/tcg/wasm64/tcg-target.c.inc
--- a/tcg/wasm64/tcg-target.c.inc
+++ b/tcg/wasm64/tcg-target.c.inc
@@ -980,10 +980,32 @@
 /* calls                                                               */
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 
-/* current code offset, for retaddr values */
+/*
+ * Retaddr marker for GETPC()-using helpers.
+ *
+ * cpu_unwind_data_from_tb() resolves a retaddr by walking the per-insn
+ * end offsets for the first one *strictly greater* than
+ * (retaddr - GETPC_ADJ): a real backend's GETPC() is a return address,
+ * which always sits after the call, i.e. strictly inside the faulting
+ * insn's code range.  Here the marker is emitted before the call
+ * sequence, and for a guest insn whose code starts with that call (any
+ * plain load/store: the address is already in a register) the raw
+ * offset equals the insn's start = the previous insn's end, so the
+ * unwind resolved one guest insn too early.  cpu_io_recompile() then
+ * rewound to the previous insn and re-executed it — an EL71 boot
+ * re-ran an `ldm r0!` twice before a buffered flash program and wrote
+ * the erased pattern, aborting with ">>EXIT<< FILE: flash" (0x0506).
+ *
+ * Bias by GETPC_ADJ so the subtraction lands exactly on the insn start,
+ * which the strict comparison attributes to this insn.  The call
+ * sequence that follows is always longer than the bias, so the marker
+ * still refers to this insn and never to the next one.
+ */
+#define W64_GETPC_ADJ 2         /* GETPC_ADJ, accel/tcg/tb-internal.h */
 static inline uintptr_t w64_pc(TCGContext *s)
 {
-    return (uintptr_t)s->code_buf + (s->code_ptr - s->code_buf);
+    return (uintptr_t)s->code_buf + (s->code_ptr - s->code_buf)
+           + W64_GETPC_ADJ;
 }
 
 /* typemask typecode -> wasm type (0 = i32, 1 = i64); 0xff invalid */
